exists su name hymn source thrust verify prompt ob text quoted.text.Verify whether LYRIC stays faithful to the source teaching in TRANSCRIPT.

GENERATOR INTENT:
- Lyrics are poetic, but concrete teachings, practices, claims, and source-grounded details must remain faithful to TRANSCRIPT.
- Metaphor and emotional framing are allowed.

Evaluate only source-grounded teaching content:
- named person or group when used as part of the teaching,
- specific practice, instruction, or discipline,
- concrete claim about what the source says or recommends,
- specific action, mechanism, image, or framing presented as part of the teaching.

Ignore pure emotional language and poetic uplift unless they add unsupported source claims.
Do not fail merely because the lyric adds fresh sensory imagery, scene-setting detail, or poetic connective tissue if the underlying teaching remains faithful.

PASS if:
- the lyric stays faithful to the source teaching in TRANSCRIPT,
- no unsupported concrete teaching claims are introduced,
- no material meaning drift occurs.

FAIL if:
- concrete teaching or source claims lack support,
- unsupported doctrinal or source-specific details are added,
- the teaching meaning is materially altered.

Output rules:
- First output one short paragraph (1-2 sentences, max 70 words).
- Final line must be exactly PASS or FAIL.
- No bullets, no labels, no markdown.
- No text after the final verdict line..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name hymn source thrust verdict prompt ob text quoted.text.Read the verifier analysis and output exactly one word: PASS or FAIL.

Rules:
